{"events":[{"tStartMs":0,"dDurationMs":13800,"segs":[{"utf8":"Five things happened in open source this week, one of them is a licence change that is going to matter for a long time, and one is a terminal tool I did not expect to like."}]},{"tStartMs":13800,"dDurationMs":11200,"segs":[{"utf8":"The first is a release that finally lands incremental parsing in the editor core, which means the syntax tree updates on the edited range instead of the whole buffer."}]},{"tStartMs":25000,"dDurationMs":12300,"segs":[{"utf8":"The maintainers spent the better part of two years on it and the pull request itself is worth reading, because the benchmark discussion in the comments is better than the release notes."}]},{"tStartMs":37300,"dDurationMs":11200,"segs":[{"utf8":"On a fifty thousand line file the reparse went from about four hundred milliseconds to under ten, and the typing latency graph in the thread makes that very obvious."}]},{"tStartMs":48500,"dDurationMs":9600,"segs":[{"utf8":"Second, a compression library that ships inside more or less everything moved from a permissive licence to a source available one with a revenue threshold."}]},{"tStartMs":58100,"dDurationMs":10400,"segs":[{"utf8":"Forks appeared within a day, which tells you exactly how much of the ecosystem was quietly depending on it without anybody sponsoring the two people maintaining it."}]},{"tStartMs":68500,"dDurationMs":9200,"segs":[{"utf8":"The interesting part is not the licence, it is that three distributions had to decide their policy in public in about thirty six hours."}]},{"tStartMs":77700,"dDurationMs":8500,"segs":[{"utf8":"Third, a vulnerability in an image parser that sits inside three different package managers, patched the same day the advisory went out."}]},{"tStartMs":86200,"dDurationMs":12300,"segs":[{"utf8":"The exploit needs a crafted file to be parsed, so it is not a wormable thing, but it is a good reminder of how deep that parser is buried in build tooling."}]},{"tStartMs":98500,"dDurationMs":10400,"segs":[{"utf8":"Fourth, a new terminal multiplexer that does panes and tabs without a config file, which sounds like a small thing until you set up a fresh machine."}]},{"tStartMs":108900,"dDurationMs":11500,"segs":[{"utf8":"I have been running it for a week and I have not missed my old setup once, although I have also not tried to do anything clever with layouts yet."}]},{"tStartMs":120400,"dDurationMs":10800,"segs":[{"utf8":"Fifth, the documentation site for a fairly large database rewrote its getting started page, and the before and after is a lesson in where people actually drop off."}]},{"tStartMs":131200,"dDurationMs":10000,"segs":[{"utf8":"The old page lost readers at step three every single time, which turned out to be a paragraph that assumed you had already created a user."}]},{"tStartMs":141200,"dDurationMs":9600,"segs":[{"utf8":"The newsletter goes out on Fridays with every link from this week plus the ones that did not make the video, and it is free."}]},{"tStartMs":150800,"dDurationMs":8500,"segs":[{"utf8":"Subscribe here if you want the long version with the actual commit links, because that is where most of the reading is."}]},{"tStartMs":159300,"dDurationMs":4200,"segs":[{"utf8":"That is the week, and I will see you on Friday."}]}]}